560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340564 13194139535264 true] [17592186340560 1110 #uuid "bedf04e9-d7bf-5602-b64b-2ddda76e45cc" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340561 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060869/assets/5b4684361e541532d1be24de046f17201811146fbb0413222c5100e5a3eb80dc.png" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535264 true] [17592186340561 1111 #uuid "0b6a1c65-f37c-5066-bd90-a071b3173300" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340562 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060869/assets/d187f89ab21a36c6709422c48263541df1acc8568d436614502c001cf576b426.png" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535264 true] [17592186340562 1111 #uuid "baacd767-ead2-5530-b180-fb6db108d7a5" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340563 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060869/assets/4bf42e3bdeb61feccd68cf4eeb9e3c4a40e8b903a5739df77c993e9aa4abc993.png" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535264 true] [17592186340563 1111 #uuid "43f27e3e-bdaa-5848-93e4-380c0f7ae3de" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340564 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060869/assets/e3fe0bfa8161108c3d5edc48a6df4a52fe2c5b4dbf1c9964cf82e4f257ff357c.png" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535264 true] [17592186340564 1111 #uuid "d7e25558-4756-59e5-b570-814c7b5307a8" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340565 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060869/assets/742f0204ee7817972e5005f2c107c4032d34266e7c75c56c5882beafe615b7d5.png" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535264 true] [17592186340565 1111 #uuid "abe0ae83-fdd2-585f-92af-b3ca476b9788" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340566 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340567 13194139535264 true] [17592186340566 1089 "q-8395" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340566 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535264 true] [17592186340566 1100 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(0,2),(3,0),(0,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(0,-3)$\n- $(0,0)$\n- $(2,0)$" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340566 1113 #uuid "64807bce-8910-5125-8156-b8d41249d50d" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340566 1145 "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${270}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,0),(0,-3),(0,0).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340568 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340569 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340570 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340571 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340572 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1041 "selection" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340568 13194139535264 true] [17592186340567 1110 #uuid "888ade6e-effd-5589-aef7-30baa528a74b" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340568 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340568 1111 #uuid "807311d1-597b-5a56-bbd3-5f82ed06d1df" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340569 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340569 1111 #uuid "3ef07423-c4e5-50c2-907f-f899fd9e3b7d" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340570 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340570 1111 #uuid "1e246d1b-17b2-59e0-b040-5c4e94399c11" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340571 1034 "III only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340571 1111 #uuid "534d6547-328a-556f-88cb-e2ad4328067e" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340572 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340572 1111 #uuid "8993f2b7-74c2-5458-b779-d3769e2d3e3c" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340573 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340574 13194139535264 true] [17592186340573 1089 "q-8396" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340573 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535264 true] [17592186340573 1100 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,1),(3,3),(4,4).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n\n- $(-2,-1)$\n- $(-3,-2)$\n- $(-3,-3)$" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340573 1113 #uuid "710f2c3e-7b35-5214-9260-d407a9299223" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340573 1145 "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,-1),(-3,-3),(-4,-4).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340575 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340576 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340577 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340578 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340579 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1041 "selection" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340576 13194139535264 true] [17592186340574 1110 #uuid "b408b6e4-f130-57a4-bd24-03be06b646b7" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340575 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340575 1111 #uuid "a9706358-eb4c-5f2e-8c57-f0d3b8be1d5d" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340576 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340576 1111 #uuid "9309c739-6725-5037-b4f9-3ae7637d8029" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340577 1034 "I only" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535264 true] [17592186340577 1111 #uuid "0a426275-b82e-5ec8-a375-2ac1b322dc5a" 13194139535264 true] [17592186340578 1034 "III only" 13194139535264 t